WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Привет, Фрэнс, welcome to привет, русский эпизод Тертии.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.640
It's 24 мая 2006 года.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:12.780
I'm Olya, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words about space.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:13.400
Ready?

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.300
Поехали?

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.840
That means let's go.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.160
Our word of the day is cosmos, cosmos.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.760
Say it with me slowly, cosmos.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.440
Now at natural speed, cosmos.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.980
It sounds exactly like the English word cosmos, and it means space.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.880
We can use it in a simple sentence, merely team of cosmos.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.260
That means we are flying to space.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.340
Repeat after me, merely team of cosmos.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.840
Now that we know the word for space, let's look at what's inside it.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.960
The next word is звезда, звезда, repeat after me, звезда.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.660
It means star, and you can picture as звез, sparkling in the night sky.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.380
Say it again, звезда.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.460
Our next word connects right to the last one, планета.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.680
Планетя, repeat after me, планета.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.600
It means planet, and it sounds just like the English word planet.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.320
We can say земля это планета.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.260
That means earth is a planet.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.460
Next comes raketa, raketa, repeat after me, raketa.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.200
It means rocket.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.260
And you can hear the engine roar in raketa.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.480
Say it once more, raketa.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.980
Now we have lunar, lunar, repeat after me, lunar.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.700
It means moon, and it glows like a lunatic night.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.180
Try it again, lunar.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.340
The sun belongs here to, солнце, солнце.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.580
Repeat after me, солнце.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.620
It means sun, and it starts with solar power.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.960
Say it slowly, солнце.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.820
Our last words are close to English.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.040
Mars, Mars.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.800
Repeat after me, Mars.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.280
It means Mars, the same name we use in English.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:59.220
And finally, astronaut, astronaut, repeat after me, astronaut.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.680
It means astronaut, and they explore the stars.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.500
Russian nouns have genders that change how we describe them.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:07.920
Take the words везда.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:12.060
It is feminine, so we say, большая звезда, for big star.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:16.760
Mars is masculine, so we say, большой Mars, for big Mars.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.540
English adjectives stay the same, but Russian ones shift to match the noun.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:26.300
Once you learn the three gender groups, it feels like sorting toys by color.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.520
Now you can say, большая звезда, or большой Mars with confidence.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.740
This small habit helps your Russian sound natural right away.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.660
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.160
The Russian word planeta, and the English word planet, are actually the same word.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.540
They both come from the ancient Greek planetis, meaning wanderer.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.660
The Greeks notice planets moving across the sky, unlike fixed stars.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.800
This word traveled through Latin into many languages, and reached Russian centuries ago.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:02.580
Be careful, though, because Luna sounds like lunar, yet simply means moon on its own.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.540
Next time you see the English word planet, remember it is cousins with the Russian planeta.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:13.140
That ancient Greek wanderer idea is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.560
Russians have a proud history of space exploration.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.960
The first human in space was cosmonaut Yuri Gagarin in 1961.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.180
Many Russian children grow up dreaming of becoming cosmonauts.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:29.600
They learn about the stars through school programs and planetariums.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.700
Do you remember what planeta means?

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.860
Try using the word звезда three times today.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.880
For kids, draw a simple picture of the sun, moon and the rocket.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.620
Then label each with the Russian words while saying them out loud.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:49.880
For adults, look up at the night sky tonight and practice saying «это звезда» or «марс-планета».

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:50.420
Молодец.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.080
That means well done.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:55.160
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.880
Practice saying today's words out loud, even just once, and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.120
See you next time.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.000
That's Russian for By.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:07.640
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.480
Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
